{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Worker workflows the pump may dispatch. A workflow is dispatched only when enabled is true. versions, image_digest and settings_state go into every run_key, so changing any of them makes every subject due again for that workflow. Lease and slot expiry = 1.5 x (setup_minutes + shard_size x minutes_per_subject) + 10 minutes. slots_max caps open dispatches for the workflow. enabled and runs_untrusted must be true or false. runs_untrusted says whether the workflow runs third-party code (servers, builds); a workflow that does not say false counts as true, and none of those is dispatched while the sandbox breaker is open (pump/breaker.mjs, docs/OPERATIONS.md). sandbox_sha is the isokron-ai/mcp-surface-corpus commit such a workflow pins its sandbox at (null until it pins one); the watchdog shows amber while it differs from the commit the nightly conformance run tested. pin_check (\"label\" or \"enforce\"; R-PIN-01, pump/pins.mjs) says how the tool and probe versions are made true: ingest refuses a result whose manifest reports another version than the run_key is filed under on every lane, and on an enforce lane also one that does not prove each pinned version; on an enforce lane whose versions.tool pins a commit of the worker repository itself (the entry named after the repository), the pump sends that full commit as the tool_sha input and the worker must run it. label is for worker repositories that do not run and report their pins yet. sha_check (\"label\", the default, or \"enforce\"; R-SHA-01, pump/pins.mjs) says what ingest does when the commit a worker says it read (manifest subject.sha) is not the commit the run_key names: label records it in the report, enforce refuses the result as subject_sha_mismatch; a refusal never parks the run_key, it waits the retry backoff. send_sha (true or false, default false; R-SHA-05) sends each item its run_key's commit (items[].sha), only to a worker that reads exactly that commit; sha_check \"enforce\" needs send_sha true. The worker contract is in docs/INTERFACES.md. A control lane (control_subjects, dispatch_style \"t0\", switch; pump/controls.mjs) drives T0 workers on our own fixtures and servers: it is dispatched only while the repository variable named by `switch` is exactly \"true\", takes one subject per dispatch, and a miss is a lead against our tool, never the subject's.",
